From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] theme: keep native corners on tiled windows

Tiling places windows with gaps between them, so a tiled window is a
floating card like any other and keeps its corners. Only fullscreen
windows meet the display edge. Tiled windows still draw no outer
shadow (0032), so their surface extents match the tile exactly.

--- a/src/stylesheet/widgets/_window.scss
+++ b/src/stylesheet/widgets/_window.scss
@@ -107,6 +107,17 @@
     outline: none;
   }
 
+  // Tiled windows sit in a gapped layout and keep the same corners.
+  &.csd.tiled:not(.fullscreen),
+  &.csd.tiled-top:not(.fullscreen),
+  &.csd.tiled-left:not(.fullscreen),
+  &.csd.tiled-right:not(.fullscreen),
+  &.csd.tiled-bottom:not(.fullscreen) {
+    --window-radius: 15px;
+    border-radius: var(--window-radius);
+    outline: none;
+  }
+
   &.solid-csd {
     margin: 0;
     padding: 5px;
